<title>SPAIN: Bayer says to merge Spain, Portugal units.</title>
<headline>Bayer says to merge Spain, Portugal units.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayer AG's Spanish unit said on Monday that the Spanish and Portuguese units of the German chemicals group would be merged into an Iberia region, although each would retain its legal identity.</p>
<p>Bayer said that it had already grouped businesses in the Benelux, Scandinavia, Baltic countries and the U.K. and Ireland.</p>
<p>The new structure would take better advantage of growth opportunities on the Iberian peninsula, it said</p>
<p>Bayer Espana posted consolidated gross profit of 15.6 billion pesetas in 1996.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
